  "notes": "Arithmetic in memory: N memory banks, each with one multiply-accumulate unit at its edge, driven by one command sequencer that issues one command per cycle to all banks. Row r of A is written into bank r; for each column of B a fill command broadcasts the column into every unit's register file, N reads each multiply and accumulate the open row's next entry, and the result is kept; then the results are written back through the row buffer and read out to C. Each multiplier forms an unsigned product and subtracts a sign correction. N multipliers in total; latency N*N + N + 6 (26 at N = 4).",
  "player": "bankmole",
